# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#162), L §2.5 Keys and L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees: a bare y that no index, axis or thing
# holds, with no position to name its index, is LOAD-KEY at load, whatever the asks: a's law is a hole, so nothing
# inside it is evaluated (L §5.11), and the reality is still refused. 2.1.7's refcore met it only where a read
# evaluated it (a printed the law's hole, b 1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input dd: date
input n: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 1 "s"

ask a: y law dd
ask b: n
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY ambiguous key y (m.tally:17)
